<title>NETHERLANDS: Fortis declines comment on French CIC talk.</title>
<headline>Fortis declines comment on French CIC talk.</headline>
<dateline>UTRECHT, Netherlands 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch-Belgian financial group Fortis declined comment on a report of Dutch news agency ANP indicating it was one of seven candidates left to bid for French Credit Industriel et Commercial (CIC).</p>
<p>&quot;We never talk about possible acquisitions,&quot; said a Fortis spokesman, adding he would not confirm whether Fortis was in the running to acquire CIC.</p>
<p>ANP named Societe Generale and Credit Mutual as two other candidates possibly in the running for CIC.</p>
<p>The French government launched a tender on August 6 for the sale of 67 percent of CIC, which is owned by state-controlled insurer Groupe des Assurances Nationales, which itself is a candidate for privatisation once CIC is sold off.</p>
